# Google "Continue with Google" — iOS OAuth client ID
#
# This client ID is the platform-specific OAuth client used by
# GoogleSignIn-iOS to launch the consent flow from the app.
#
# To set up:
#   1. Visit https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials and
#      create an "iOS" OAuth 2.0 Client ID. Bundle ID must match the
#      Wisp iOS bundle identifier (see "PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER" in
#      wisp.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj).
#   2. Copy the resulting client ID (looks like
#      1234567890-abc...xyz.apps.googleusercontent.com) into
#      wisp/Resources/google-ios-client-id.txt (no quotes, single line).
#   3. ALSO register the reversed URL scheme so the OAuth redirect can
#      re-enter the app. In Xcode:
#         Target wisp → Info → URL Types → +
#         URL Schemes:  com.googleusercontent.apps.<reversed-id>
#         (the "reversed" form is the client ID with its components in
#         reverse; Google Cloud Console shows it directly).
#   4. Add the SPM dependency in Xcode if not already added:
#         File → Add Package Dependencies…
#         https://github.com/google/GoogleSignIn-iOS
#         Add GoogleSignIn (and optionally GoogleSignInSwift) to the
#         wisp target.
#   5. Add the "Google G" mark asset to Assets.xcassets as `GoogleG`
#      (Google's brand guidelines require their official G mark on
#      "Sign in with Google" / "Continue with Google" buttons —
#      download from https://developers.google.com/identity/branding-guidelines).
#
# This file (the .example) is checked in. The real file
# (google-ios-client-id.txt) is gitignored.
